          "text": "There are three types of connective tissue fibers: collagen, reticular, and elastic.\n\nType I collagen forms the bulk of the lamina propria and provides the tensile strength to the gingival tissue.\n\nThe elastic fiber system is composed of oxytalan, elaunin, and elastin fibers distributed among collagen fibers."
