          "text": "Shallow crevice or space around the tooth coronal to the attachment of the junctional epithelium and bounded by the tooth on one side and the sulcular epithelium on the other. The coronal extent of the gingival sulcus is the gingival margin.\n\nThe gingival sulcus contains a fluid that seeps into it from the gingival connective tissue through the thin sulcular epithelium. Functions of gingival fluid: - cleanse material from the sulcus - contain plasma proteins that may improve adhesion of the epithelium to the tooth - possess antimicrobial properties - exert antibody activity to defend the gingiva"
