        {
          "ref": [
            17,
            7
          ],
          "text": "Periodontal Abcess\nAcute or Chronic\nu  Acute: Localized, throbbing and\ncontinuous pain unaffected by thermal\nchange, sensitivity of the tooth to\npercussion and tooth mobility. The\nabscess appears as an ovoid elevation\nof the gingiva along the lateral aspect\nof the root.\nu  Chronic: A localized swelling is present\nin the gingiva somewhere along the\nlength of the root with a sinus\nformation. The orifice of the sinus may\nbe covered by a small pink nodule or a\nbead-like mass of soft hemorrhagic\ngranulation tissue. The chronic abscess\nis usually asymptomatic.  It often\nundergoes acute exacerbation."
        }
