          "text": "11/14/25\nPeriodontal\nClinical Case                                          Case 1\nPresentation\nVera W. L. Tang, DDS, MS, FICD\nDiplomate, American Board of Periodontology\nVice Chair, Periodontology & Implant Dentistry\nDirector, Pre-Doctoral Periodontology\nPatient/Chief Complaint\nMr. Potato Head, a 60-year-old cynical potato-shaped doll with put-together\npieces on his body.\nHe presents to the clinic for a routine check-up.\nHis chief complaint is that ”food keeps getting stuck in between my teeth”.\nHistory (Vitals, Medical, Dental, Family, Social, Medication)\n•  Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (T2DM) for 12 years ago controlled with\nMetformin.\n• No known drug allergy/sensitivity\n•  Vitals are BP RAS 162/97 pulse 66 and respiration rate 25.\n•  Labs 2 months ago: fast blood glucose 189mg/dL, HbA1c 8.7%.\n•  Dental treatment: last visit 2 year ago.\n•  History of non-surgical periodontal therapy about 3 years ago and\northodontics therapy as a child.\n•  Smokes 1 pack of cigarettes per day for the past 15 years.\nClinical Presentation                     Plaque & Calculus"
